{"slug": "fung-gow-pork-and-peanut-dumplings", "nyt_id": 2346, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/2346-fung-gow-pork-and-peanut-dumplings", "name": "Fung Gow: (Pork And Peanut Dumplings)", "author": "Craig Claiborne", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "42 dumplings", "min": 42, "max": 42, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 35, "raw": {"total": "35 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 pound ground pork", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "ground pork", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 tablespoon cornstarch", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "cornstarch", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "¼ cup water", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 cups plus 1 tablespoon of corn, peanut or vegetable oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "plus 1 tablespoon of corn", "preparation": "peanut or vegetable oil", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 tablespoon finely minced garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "finely minced garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "¾ cup finely chopped celery", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped celery", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "¾ cup finely chopped bamboo shoots", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped bamboo shoots", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 teaspoon salt, if desired", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": "if desired", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 ½ teaspoons sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "¼ teaspoon freshly ground pepper, preferably white", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "freshly ground pepper", "preparation": "preferably white", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "½ teaspoon sesame oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "sesame oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 cup coarsely chopped fresh coriander leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "coarsely chopped fresh coriander leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "¼ cup roasted peanuts", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "roasted peanuts", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "3 cups wheat starch, available in Oriental grocery stores", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "wheat starch", "preparation": "available in Oriental grocery stores", "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "1 ½ cups boiling water", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "boiling water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "To prepare the filling, put the pork in a mixing bowl. Blend the cornstarch with ¼ cup water and add to pork. Blend well."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Place a sieve inside a bowl and have it ready."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Heat two cups of the oil in a wok and when it is very hot add the pork mixture. Cook, stirring rapidly, about three minutes. Pour the pork and oil into the sieve and drain."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Heat the remaining tablespoon of fresh oil in a clean wok and add the garlic. Cook briefly, stirring. Add the celery and bamboo shoots and cook, stirring rapidly, about one minute. Add the cooked pork and stir quickly to blend."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Blend the salt, sugar, pepper and sesame oil. Add this to the pork and stir. Cook about one minute, stirring, over high heat. Spoon and scrape the pork mixture onto a flat plate. Sprinkle with chopped coriander and peanuts and let cool. Toss to blend."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Put the wheat starch in a mixing bowl and add the boiling water, stirring rapidly. The dough may seem a trifle dry, but on kneading it will become a stiff, workable mass. Turn the dough out onto a flat surface and knead rapidly about four or five minutes. Sprinkle the surface lightly with wheat starch as you knead. Shape the dough into a long rope or sausage shape about half an inch thick. Cut the dough crosswise into 42 pieces of equal length, each about two inches wide."}, {"position": 7, "text": "Using a rolling pin, roll each piece of dough into a circle and each circle into a thin round, three inches in diameter."}, {"position": 8, "text": "Fill each round of dough with about three and one half teaspoons of the filling. Fold the sides of each circle over to make a half-moon shape. Press the tops of each with the fingers to seal. If desired, pleat the tops of each to make a fancy shape."}, {"position": 9, "text": "Bring water to a boil in the bottom of a steamer."}, {"position": 10, "text": "As the dumplings are prepared, arrange them in a steamer rack without crowding and place over boiling water. Cover closely and steam about four minutes. Serve if desired with vinegar, soy sauce, Sichuan paste sauce and hot mustard."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 168.6, "protein_g": 2.2, "carbohydrates_g": 9.1, "fat_g": 13.8, "saturated_fat_g": 1.6, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 7.8, "sodium_mg": 64.6, "fiber_g": 0.3, "sugar_g": 0.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 11.4, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["chinese"], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["peanut", "pork", "steam", "stir-fry"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 10}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1986-10-01", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T04:21:48.831375+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "furikake-egg-salad-sandwich", "nyt_id": 782838651, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/782838651-furikake-egg-salad-sandwich", "name": "Furikake Egg Salad Sandwich", "author": "Ifrah F. Ahmed", "description": "This egg salad sandwich is an umami-filled dream. Slices of soft bread are filled with a mayo-rich and Dijon-spiked egg mixture that gets an herby lift from chopped dill and the satisfying sea-like flavor of furikake. Briny pickle juice lends a punch along with sharp minced red onion. These flavors come together to make a sandwich that is a perfect lunch or snack for any warm day, whether you enjoy it while standing at the kitchen counter or picnicking at the beach. Pair it with the potato chips of your choice and a juicy pickle or serve it on its own. Just make sure to chill the egg salad filling for at least 10 minutes before assembling the sandwiches.", "servings": {"text": "4 sandwiches", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 5, "cook_minutes": 20, "total_minutes": 25, "raw": {"total": "25 min", "prep": "PT0H5M", "cook": "PT0H20M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "8 large hard-boiled eggs, cooled", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large hard-boiled eggs", "preparation": "cooled", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ cup mayonnaise", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "mayonnaise", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons minced red onion", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "minced red onion", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 tablespoons chopped fresh dill", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh dill", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 tablespoon pickle brine", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "pickle brine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1½ teaspoons Dijon mustard", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "½ teaspoons dijon mustard", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "¼ teaspoon fine sea salt", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "fine sea salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Black pepper, to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "black pepper", "preparation": "to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 tablespoons furikake (such as nori komi), plus more for serving, if desired", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "furikake (such as nori komi)", "preparation": "plus more for serving, if desired", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "8 slices Japanese milk bread or sourdough", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "slice", "item": "japanese milk bread or sourdough", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Pickles and potato chips, for serving (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "pickles and potato chips", "preparation": "for serving", "optional": true}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Peel eggs and chop into small bite-size pieces (you should have about 3 cups). Transfer to a medium bowl and mix in the mayonnaise, red onion, dill, pickle brine, mustard, salt, black pepper and furikake. Taste and season with additional salt and pepper as needed. Chill egg salad in the fridge for 10 minutes or until you are ready to assemble sandwiches."}, {"position": 2, "text": "To assemble, spread the egg salad on four slices of bread. Top with extra furikake if desired, then top with the remaining slices of bread to make sandwiches. Serve with pickles and potato chips on the side, if desired."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 521.0, "protein_g": 19.2, "carbohydrates_g": 29.9, "fat_g": 35.7, "saturated_fat_g": 7.0, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 384.3, "sodium_mg": 588.9, "fiber_g": 2.7, "sugar_g": 4.7, "unsaturated_fat_g": 25.9, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["japanese inspired"], "diet": ["alcohol-free", "peanut-free", "pescatarian", "pork-free", "shellfish-free", "tree nut-free", "soy-free", "dairy-free"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["lunch", "snack"], "occasion": ["picnic"], "other": ["egg", "mayonnaise", "red onion", "dill", "egg salad", "sandwiches", "no cook", "easy", "make-ahead", "quick", "summer"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/06/25/multimedia/IFA-Furikake-Egg-Salad-Sandwich-mbfz/IFA-Furikake-Egg-Salad-Sandwich-mbfz-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 152}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2026-06-30", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:12:17.863781+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "fusilli-with-tomatoes-eggplant-and-pine-nuts", "nyt_id": 7044, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/7044-fusilli-with-tomatoes-eggplant-and-pine-nuts", "name": "Fusilli With Tomatoes, Eggplant and Pine Nuts", "author": "Moira Hodgson", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 main-course servings, 8 first-course servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 60, "raw": {"total": "1 hour"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 eggplant", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "eggplant", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "Coarse salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "coarse salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "3 tablespoons olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 clove garlic, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 pound fusilli", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "fusilli", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 tablespoons chopped fresh oregano", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh oregano", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ cup pitted black olives", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "pitted black olives", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "4 large ripe tomatoes, seeded and chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large ripe tomatoes", "preparation": "seeded and chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "½ cup toasted pine nuts", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "toasted pine nuts", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "Freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Freshly grated Parmesan", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly grated parmesan", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Slice the eggplant and sprinkle with salt. Leave them for 30 minutes, then pat them dry with paper towels."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Preheat grill or broiler. Brush the eggplant slices on both sides with olive oil and sprinkle them with garlic. Grill them until tender and set aside. When the eggplant has cooled, chop it into half-inch pieces."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Meanwhile, bring six quarts salted water to a rolling boil and add the fusilli. Cook until al dente."}, {"position": 4, "text": "While the pasta is cooking, chop the oregano and saute it in the remaining olive oil for one to two minutes. Add the olives, tomatoes and eggplant and heat them through."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Drain the fusilli. Put the sauce in a heated serving bowl and add the pasta. Toss well and add the pine nuts. Season with salt and pepper and serve. Freshly grated Parmesan cheese should be passed separately."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 741.5, "protein_g": 22.8, "carbohydrates_g": 104.4, "fat_g": 27.6, "saturated_fat_g": 4.1, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 4.8, "sodium_mg": 1066.6, "fiber_g": 11.5, "sugar_g": 12.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 20.5, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian"], "diet": ["vegetarian"], "course": ["appetizer", "main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["boil", "broil", "easy", "eggplant", "pasta", "pastas", "pine nut", "saute", "summer", "tomato", "weeknight"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 13}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1995-09-10", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:58:36.283500+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "fuyu-persimmon-salad", "nyt_id": 12897, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12897-fuyu-persimmon-salad", "name": "Fuyu Persimmon Salad", "author": "David Tanis", "description": "The Fuyu persimmon, round and squat and rather tomato-shaped, is the kind you can eat raw. You want to buy the ones that have turned truly orange (if they are greenish-gold, let them ripen for a few days), then peel them and slice them. The flesh is firm but sweet. Eat them plain, in the Japanese fashion, with a pot of tea. Fuyus persimmons make wonderful salads, too.", "servings": {"text": "4 to 6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "About 20 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 shallot, finely diced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "shallot", "preparation": "finely diced", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "Salt and pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 tablespoon sherry vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sherry vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "3 Fuyu persimmons", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "fuyu persimmons", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ cup thinly sliced tender celery stalks and leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "thinly sliced tender celery stalks and leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 head radicchio, leaves torn into 2-inch wide ribbons", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "head", "item": "radicchio", "preparation": "leaves torn into 2-inch wide ribbons", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "Chunk of Parmesan, for shaving", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "chunk of parmesan", "preparation": "for shaving", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Make the vinaigrette: put diced shallot in a small bowl with a pinch of salt. Add lemon juice and sherry vinegar and leave to macerate for about 5 minutes. Stir in olive oil. Season with additional salt and pepper to taste."}, {"position": 2, "text": "With a sharp paring knife, remove and discard the leafy calyx at the top of each persimmon. Peel persimmons and cut in half vertically. Lay persimmons flat side down and cut into ½-inch wedges."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Put persimmon wedges and celery slices in a low, wide salad bowl. Season with salt and pepper. Whisk vinaigrette, then pour over persimmon and celery and toss to coat well. Add radicchio and toss lightly."}, {"position": 4, "text": "With a vegetable peeler, shave about 1 ounce of Parmesan in thin strips over salad."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 147.7, "protein_g": 4.1, "carbohydrates_g": 7.8, "fat_g": 11.5, "saturated_fat_g": 2.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 6.5, "sodium_mg": 179.2, "fiber_g": 0.7, "sugar_g": 1.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 8.3, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["american"], "diet": ["vegetarian"], "course": ["side dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["celery", "easy", "fall", "persimmon", "quick", "radicchio", "salad", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2012/10/31/dining/31KITCH1_SPAN/31KITCH1_SPAN-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 157}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2012-10-31", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:01:43.500439+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
